{number: 12}
{title: Come, Thou Almighty King}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Come, Thou al-[G] mighty [C] King,
[F] Help us Thy [C] name to [G] sing,
[C] Help us to [G] praise:
[C] Father, all [G] glorious,
[C] O'er all vic-[G] torious,
[C] Come and reign [F] over us,
[C] Ancient of [G] Days! [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Come, Thou In-[G] carnate [C] Word,
[F] Gird on Thy [C] mighty [G] sword,
[C] Our prayer at-[G] tend:
[C] Come, and Thy [G] people bless,
[C] And give Thy [G] Word success;
[C] Spirit of [F] holiness,
[C] On us de-[G] scend! [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Come, Holy [G] Comfor-[C] ter,
[F] Thy sacred [C] witness [G] bear
[C] In this glad [G] hour:
[C] Thou Who al-[G] mighty art,
[C] Now rule in [G] every heart,
[C] And ne'er from [F] us depart,
[C] Spirit of [G] power! [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] To the great [G] One in [C] Three
[F] Eternal [C] praises [G] be,
[C] Hence ever-[G] more:
[C] His sovereign [G] majesty
[C] May we in [G] glory see,
[C] And to e-[F] ternity
[C] Love and a-[G] dore! [C]
{end_of_verse}
